---
import PolicyPage from "../components/PolicyPage.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  path="/privacy/"
  description="What personal information PTO Info Daily collects, why, and your rights under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023."
  intro="This policy explains what personal information we collect when you use PTO Info Daily, why we collect it, and the rights you have over it."
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} ({SITE.url}) is a digital news publication based in{" "}
    {SITE.location}. We are responsible for the personal information
    described in this policy. We handle personal data in line with the
    Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023.
  </p>

  <h2>Readers</h2>
  <p>
    You can read {SITE.name} without creating an account. We do not ask
    readers for their name or contact details, and we do not currently use
    advertising or tracking cookies.
  </p>
  <p>When you visit the website, some technical information is processed automatically:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting and security.</strong> Our website is hosted on
      Cloudflare. To deliver pages and protect the site from abuse,
      Cloudflare processes technical data such as your IP address, browser
      type and the pages you request.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fonts.</strong> Our pages load typefaces from Google Fonts,
      which means your browser connects to Google's servers and shares your
      IP address with Google.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>People who contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us — for example to request a correction, share a story
    tip or make a complaint — we receive your email address, your name if
    you include it, and the contents of your message. We use this only to
    respond to you and deal with your request, and we keep it only as long
    as needed for that purpose and our records.
  </p>

  <h2>Writers and editors</h2>
  <p>
    Members of our editorial team who use our writers' portal have an
    account with their name, email address, role and a securely hashed
    password (we never store passwords in readable form). When they sign
    in, we set a single essential cookie to keep them signed in. For
    security, we also record recent sign-in attempts (email address, IP
    address and time) to protect accounts from password-guessing attacks.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The only cookie we set is the essential sign-in cookie used by our
    editorial team in the writers' portal. Readers do not receive this
    cookie. If we introduce analytics or advertising in future, we will
    update this policy and ask for your consent where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use personal data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>to run, secure and improve the website;</li>
    <li>to respond to messages, corrections and complaints;</li>
    <li>to manage our editorial team's accounts; and</li>
    <li>to meet our legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>

  <h2>Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We share personal information only with service providers that help us
    operate the website (such as Cloudflare for hosting and Google for
    fonts), or where we are required to do so by law. Some of these
    providers process data outside Nigeria; where that happens we rely on
    them to protect it appropriately.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>be informed about how your personal data is used;</li>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
    <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
    <li>have your data deleted in certain circumstances;</li>
    <li>restrict or object to how we use your data;</li>
    <li>withdraw consent where we rely on consent;</li>
    <li>receive your data in a portable format in certain circumstances; and</li>
    <li>complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (NDPC).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To use any of these rights, email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.editorialEmail}?subject=Privacy%20request`}>{SITE.editorialEmail}</a>{" "}
    with the subject line "Privacy request". We may need to confirm your
    identity before acting on a request.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect
    personal information, including encrypted connections, hashed
    passwords, limited staff access and protection against repeated
    sign-in attempts. No online service is completely secure, but we work
    to keep your information safe.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of
    this page shows when it was last changed.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
